    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "[ Lesson 11 ]"
    },
    {
      "type": "sentences",
      "items": [
        {
          "n": "1",
          "text": "Whom do you live with?"
        },
        {
          "n": "2",
          "text": "He came with a book."
        },
        {
          "n": "3",
          "text": "He has a poor relationship with her."
        },
        {
          "n": "4",
          "text": "The money is on the table with the shopping list."
        },
        {
          "n": "5",
          "text": "With only two days to go, we can't delay it."
        },
        {
          "n": "6",
          "text": "With the Asian economy in recession, the IMF is demanding structural reforms."
        },
        {
          "n": "7",
          "text": "With all her faults, he still liked her."
        },
        {
          "n": "8",
          "text": "I walked through a crowd."
        },
        {
          "n": "9",
          "text": "He travelled through China."
        },
        {
          "n": "10",
          "text": "It is not the role of the teacher."
        },
        {
          "n": "11",
          "text": "He accused her of lying."
        },
        {
          "n": "12",
          "text": "He informed me of the incident."
        },
        {
          "n": "13",
          "text": "What do you think of it?"
        },
        {
          "n": "14",
          "text": "He lived in a village 10 miles north of Seoul."
        },
        {
          "n": "15",
          "text": "The office is in the southern Texas city of Dallas."
        },
        {
          "n": "16",
          "text": "He walked to the office."
        },
        {
          "n": "17",
          "text": "Wait until the traffic lights change from red to green."
        },
        {
          "n": "18",
          "text": "He gave it to his sister."
        },
        {
          "n": "19",
          "text": "This is the solution to the problem."
        },
        {
          "n": "20",
          "text": "You can go to prison for drunken driving."
        }
      ]
    },
